# Week 1

This week I learned how to use the command line. I learned how to create
folders, files, and navigate using the command line. I made a simple HTML
page using the file editor Atom and the command line.

## The command line

In order to learn how to use the command line, I had to first figure out how
to create folders and files using the command line.

### Creating folders and files

To create a folder, you type the following command in the command line:

`mkdir <name>`

This will make a directory with the name `<name>`.

To create a file, you type the following command in the command line:

`touch <name>`

This will make a file with the name `<name>`.

To navigate to a folder, you type the following command in the command line:

`cd <name>`

This will navigate into the folder with the name `<name>`.

## Atom

I created a simple HTML document using the file editor Atom.

