    Write a function that takes a message, and encodes in such a
    way that it swaps case of all letters, replaces all vowels in
    the message with the letter that appears 2 places ahead of that
    vowel in the english alphabet.
    Assume only letters.

    Examples:
    >>> encode("test")
    "TGST"
    >>> encode("This is a message")
    "tHKS KS C MGSSCGG"
     */
    public String encode(String message) {
	// Write your code here.
	String vowels = "aeiou";
	String newMessage = "";
	char newLetter ='';
	for (int i = 0; i < message.length(); i++) {
	    if (vowels.indexOf(message.charAt(i)) >= 0) {
		if (i == message.length() - 1) {
		    newLetter = message.charAt(0);
		}
		else {
		    newLetter = message.charAt(i + 2);
		}
	    }
	    else {
		if (Character.isLowerCase(message.charAt(i))) {
		    newLetter = Character.toUpperCase(message.charAt(i));
		}
		else if (Character.isUpperCase(message.charAt(i))) {
		    newLetter = Character.toLowerCase(message.charAt(i));
		}
		else {
		    newLetter = message.charAt(i);
		}
	    }
	    newMessage += newLetter;
	}
	return newMessage;
    }
